.TH ACTION_BIND_KEY 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
action_bind_key \- Bind action a (your own enum value, < ACTION_MAX) to a keyboard key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqactions.h\(dq
.BI "void action_bind_key(ActionMap *m, int a, Key key);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bind action a (your own enum value, < ACTION_MAX) to a keyboard key. Each action holds up to three keys, filled in order; a fourth call is ignored. Bind both arrows and WASD to the same action so either works: action_bind_key(&m, ACT_LEFT, KEY_LEFT); action_bind_key(&m, ACT_LEFT, KEY_A). To rebind, call action_map_init and bind again.
.PP
This is a static inline function; it is defined in the header.
.SH MODULE
input (src/engine/input/actions.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR action_bind_pad (3),
